Copyright 2026 Jay's FreeCAD Skill contributors

Credit where it is due: the workflow of this skill (build the model, render it from
several angles, and look at the images before handing a part over) was inspired by
the "openscad" skill in mitsuhiko/agent-stuff
(https://github.com/mitsuhiko/agent-stuff), Apache License 2.0.

The tools, the SKILL.md instructions and the example models in this repository were
written new for FreeCAD. The tool file names (validate, preview, multi-preview,
extract-params, render-with-params) match that skill's on purpose, so anyone who
knows one will recognise the other. The example parts (a lidded box and a phone
stand) are new FreeCAD designs of the same two objects, and they keep that skill's
parameter names and default sizes.
